---
description: Use ast-index for structural code search before broad text search.
alwaysApply: true
---

Use `ast-index` first for structural code navigation: files, symbols, classes,
usages, callers, implementations, refs, outlines, modules, dependencies, and
project maps.

Project MCP config sets `AST_INDEX_DB_PATH` to `${workspaceFolder}/.ast-index/index.db`.
Before the first structural query, run `ast-index stats`. If there is no usable
index, run `ast-index rebuild` from the project root. After pulling or rebasing,
run `ast-index update`.

Use `rg` instead for raw text, regex, comments, exact string literals, or when
`ast-index` returns no useful hits.

Useful commands:

```bash
ast-index search "Query"
ast-index file "FileName"
ast-index symbol "SymbolName"
ast-index class "ClassName"
ast-index usages "SymbolName"
ast-index refs "SymbolName"
ast-index outline "path/to/file.py"
```
